{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Nre68uyxBgD9ZkcHvYJDZW", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\t\"\"\"The metered tensor engine.\n2\t\n3\tEvery engine call advances one global odometer by a price that is a function of tensor shapes only, never of the\n4\tmachine or the values, so the same program reaches the same reading everywhere.\n5\t\n6\tThe unit is a tick, priced to be about one nanosecond of one laptop core. tools/calibrate.py measures nanoseconds per\n7\ttick for every op on real machines and fails if any op drifts more than a factor of 5 from the median, so an entry\n8\tcannot get cheap work by picking mispriced ops.\n9\t\n10\tPrices (v3), per call:\n11\t  * every call: 2000 ticks, the Python overhead of the call itself. Backward passes pay it again per node.\n12\t  * matmul of (..., m, k) @ (..., k, n): max(m, 8) * max(k, 64) * max(n, 8) / 128 plus 256, per batch element (a 2-D right side is one\n13\t    flat call, so m counts the batch and the 256 is paid once). The same again per input needing a gradient, with the\n14\t    inner and outer dimensions swapped to match the product backward actually does.\n15\t  * cheap elementwise work (add, mul, negate, compare, copy, sum): 1 tick per 4 elements. ones and full 1 per 8, and\n16\t    zeros and the backward of a sum 1 per 16 and 1 per 8, because they only fill memory.\n17\t  * sqrt, div, tanh: 1 tick per 2 elements. exp, log, sigmoid, sin, cos: 1 per element. where, power, sign: 2 per\n18\t    element. Integer % and //: 1 per element.\n19\t  * randn 4 and rand 2 per element. Logit ops (softmax, log_softmax, cross_entropy): 2 per logit, 1 per logit backward;\n20\t    cross_entropy pays the call price twice.\n21\t  * embedding: 1 per 4 elements, plus per row 8 and 2 per million table floats; backward 16 per element plus the zeroed\n22\t    table.\n23\t  * concat: 256 per input tensor on top of the elements, 1024 per input tensor backward. split: 2000 per part forward,\n24\t    512 per part backward. data.batch: 2000 plus 64 per row plus 1 per byte.\n25\t  * views (transpose, slicing, a reshape that keeps the memory) are free apart from the call price. A reshape that has\n26\t    to copy pays 1 per element.\n27\t\n28\tWhen a charge would pass the budget, the op raises BudgetExhausted and every later op raises too.\n29\t\"\"\"\n30\t\n31\timport contextlib as _contextlib\n32\timport math as _math\n33\t\n34\timport numpy as _np\n35\t\n36\t_F = _np.float32\n37\t_I = _np.int32\n38\t\n39\t\n40\tclass BudgetExhausted(Exception):\n41\t    pass\n42\t\n43\t\n44\tclass RuleViolation(Exception):\n45\t    pass\n46\t\n47\t\n48\tclass _Meter:\n49\t    def __init__(self):\n50\t        self.reset(None, 0)\n51\t\n52\t    def reset(self, budget, seed, mode=\"train\", item_cap=20_000):\n53\t        self.budget = budget\n54\t        self.used = 0\n55\t        self.exhausted = False\n56\t        self.mode = mode\n57\t        self.grad = mode == \"train\"\n58\t        self.items = 0\n59\t        self.item_cap = item_cap\n60\t        self.init_rng = _np.random.default_rng([seed, 0])\n61\t        self.data_rng = _np.random.default_rng([seed, 1])\n62\t\n63\t\n64\t_M = _Meter()\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t_CALL = 2000  # ticks for one engine call, whatever its size\n68\t\n69\t\n70\tdef _tick(n=0):\n71\t    if _M.exhausted:\n72\t        raise BudgetExhausted(\"the odometer already reached its budget\")\n73\t    n = int(n) if n > 0 else 0  # a negative price would run the odometer backwards\n74\t    n += _CALL\n75\t    if _M.budget is not None and _M.used + n > _M.budget:\n76\t        _M.exhausted = True\n77\t        raise BudgetExhausted(f\"budget {_M.budget:.3e} reached at {_M.used:.3e}\")\n78\t    _M.used += n\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tdef _train_only(what):\n82\t    if _M.mode != \"train\":\n83\t        raise RuleViolation(f\"{what} is not allowed during evaluation\")\n84\t\n85\t\n86\tdef used():\n87\t    return _M.used\n88\t\n89\t\n90\tdef budget():\n91\t    return _M.budget\n92\t\n93\t\n94\tdef remaining():\n95\t    return None if _M.budget is None else _M.budget - _M.used\n96\t\n97\t\n98\t@_contextlib.contextmanager\n99\tdef no_grad():\n100\t    prev = _M.grad\n101\t    _M.grad = False\n102\t    try:\n103\t        yield\n104\t    finally:\n105\t        _M.grad = prev\n106\t\n107\t\n108\tclass Tensor:\n109\t    \"\"\"An opaque array. Values leave the engine only through item(), which is rationed.\"\"\"\n110\t\n111\t    __slots__ = (\"_d\", \"_prev\", \"_back\", \"_rg\", \"grad\")\n112\t\n113\t    def __init__(self, d, prev=(), back=None, rg=False):\n114\t        self._d = d\n115\t        self._prev = prev\n116\t        self._back = back\n117\t        self._rg = rg\n118\t        self.grad = None\n119\t\n120\t    # ---- what an entry may know about a tensor\n121\t    @property\n122\t    def shape(self):\n123\t        return self._d.shape\n124\t\n125\t    @property\n126\t    def ndim(self):\n127\t        return self._d.ndim\n128\t\n129\t    @property\n130\t    def size(self):\n131\t        return int(self._d.size)\n132\t\n133\t    @property\n134\t    def is_int(self):\n135\t        return self._d.dtype.kind == \"i\"\n136\t\n137\t    @property\n138\t    def requires_grad(self):\n139\t        return self._rg\n140\t\n141\t    def __len__(self):\n142\t        return self._d.shape[0]\n143\t\n144\t    def __repr__(self):\n145\t        kind = \"int\" if self.is_int else \"float\"\n146\t        return f\"Tensor(shape={self.shape}, {kind})\"\n147\t\n148\t    __str__ = __repr__\n149\t\n150\t    def __format__(self, spec):\n151\t        return repr(self)\n152\t\n153\t    def __bool__(self):\n154\t        raise RuleViolation(\"a tensor has no truth value; use item()\")\n155\t\n156\t    def __float__(self):\n157\t        raise RuleViolation(\"use item() to read a scalar\")\n158\t\n159\t    __int__ = __index__ = __float__\n160\t\n161\t    def __iter__(self):\n162\t        raise RuleViolation(\"tensors are not iterable\")\n163\t\n164\t    def __array__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n165\t        raise RuleViolation(\"tensors cannot be converted to arrays\")\n166\t\n167\t    __hash__ = object.__hash__\n168\t\n169\t    def item(self):\n170\t        _train_only(\"item()\")\n171\t        if self._d.size != 1:\n172\t            raise RuleViolation(\"item() needs a one-element tensor\")\n173\t        _M.items += 1\n174\t        if _M.items > _M.item_cap:\n175\t            raise RuleViolation(f\"more than {_M.item_cap} item() reads\")\n176\t        _tick()\n177\t        return self._d.item()\n178\t\n179\t    def detach(self):\n180\t        return Tensor(self._d)\n181\t\n182\t    # ---- in-place update of a parameter (optimizers)\n183\t    def update(self, value):\n184\t        _train_only(\"update()\")\n185\t        value = _as_tensor(value, self)\n186\t        if value.shape != self.shape:\n187\t            value = Tensor(_np.broadcast_to(value._d, self.shape))\n188\t        _tick(self.size // 4)\n189\t        self._d[...] = value._d\n190\t\n191\t    # ---- autodiff\n192\t    def backward(self):\n193\t        _train_only(\"backward()\")\n194\t        if self.size != 1:\n195\t            raise RuleViolation(\"backward() needs a scalar loss\")\n196\t        order, seen, stack = [], set(), [(self, False)]\n197\t        while stack:\n198\t            node, done = stack.pop()\n199\t            if done:\n200\t                order.append(node)\n201\t                continue\n202\t            if id(node) in seen or not node._rg:\n203\t                continue\n204\t            seen.add(id(node))\n205\t            stack.append((node, True))\n206\t            for p in node._prev:\n207\t                stack.append((p, False))\n208\t        grads = {id(self): _np.ones_like(self._d)}\n209\t        for node in reversed(order):\n210\t            g = grads.pop(id(node), None)\n211\t            if g is None:\n212\t                continue\n213\t            if node._back is None:\n214\t                if node.grad is None:\n215\t                    node.grad = Tensor(g.astype(_F, copy=False))\n216\t                else:\n217\t                    _tick(g.size // 4)\n218\t                    node.grad._d = node.grad._d + g\n219\t                continue\n220\t            _tick()\n221\t            need = [p._rg for p in node._prev]\n222\t            for p, pg in zip(node._prev, node._back(g, need)):\n223\t                if pg is None or not p._rg:\n224\t                    continue\n225\t                if id(p) in grads:\n226\t                    _tick(pg.size // 4)\n227\t                    grads[id(p)] = grads[id(p)] + pg\n228\t                else:\n229\t                    grads[id(p)] = pg\n230\t            node._prev, node._back = (), None\n231\t\n232\t    # ---- operators\n233\t    def __add__(self, o):\n234\t        return add(self, o)\n235\t\n236\t    def __radd__(self, o):\n237\t        return add(o, self)\n238\t\n239\t    def __sub__(self, o):\n240\t        return sub(self, o)\n241\t\n242\t    def __rsub__(self, o):\n243\t        return sub(o, self)\n244\t\n245\t    def __mul__(self, o):\n246\t        return mul(self, o)\n247\t\n248\t    def __rmul__(self, o):\n249\t        return mul(o, self)\n250\t\n251\t    def __truediv__(self, o):\n252\t        return div(self, o)\n253\t\n254\t    def __rtruediv__(self, o):\n255\t        return div(o, self)\n256\t\n257\t    def __neg__(self):\n258\t        return neg(self)\n259\t\n260\t    def __pow__(self, p):\n261\t        return power(self, p)\n262\t\n263\t    def __matmul__(self, o):\n264\t        return matmul(self, o)\n265\t\n266\t    def __mod__(self, o):\n267\t        return _int_binary(self, o, _np.mod, per_4=4)\n268\t\n269\t    def __floordiv__(self, o):\n270\t        return _int_binary(self, o, _np.floor_divide, per_4=4)\n271\t\n272\t    def __gt__(self, o):\n273\t        return _compare(self, o, _np.greater)\n274\t\n275\t    def __ge__(self, o):\n276\t        return _compare(self, o, _np.greater_equal)\n277\t\n278\t    def __lt__(self, o):\n279\t        return _compare(self, o, _np.less)\n280\t\n281\t    def __le__(self, o):\n282\t        return _compare(self, o, _np.less_equal)\n283\t\n284\t    def __getitem__(self, key):\n285\t        return getitem(self, key)\n286\t\n287\t    def reshape(self, *shape):\n288\t        return reshape(self, *shape)\n289\t\n290\t    def transpose(self, *axes):\n291\t        return transpose(self, *axes)\n292\t\n293\t    def swapaxes(self, a, b):\n294\t        return swapaxes(self, a, b)\n295\t\n296\t    def sum(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n297\t        return sum(self, axis, keepdims)\n298\t\n299\t    def mean(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n300\t        return mean(self, axis, keepdims)\n301\t\n302\t    def max(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n303\t        return max(self, axis, keepdims)\n304\t\n305\t    def float(self):\n306\t        return to_float(self)\n307\t\n308\t    @property\n309\t    def T(self):\n310\t        return swapaxes(self, -1, -2)\n311\t\n312\t\n313\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- helpers\n314\t\n315\t\n316\tdef _as_tensor(x, like=None):\n317\t    if isinstance(x, Tensor):\n318\t        return x\n319\t    if isinstance(x, bool) or not isinstance(x, (int, float)):\n320\t        raise RuleViolation(f\"expected a tensor or a number, got {type(x).__name__}\")\n321\t    dtype = _I if (like is not None and like.is_int and isinstance(x, int)) else _F\n322\t    return Tensor(_np.asarray(x, dtype=dtype))\n323\t\n324\t\n325\tdef _make(d, parents, back):\n326\t    rg = _M.grad and any(p._rg for p in parents)\n327\t    return Tensor(d, parents if rg else (), back if rg else None, rg)\n328\t\n329\t\n330\tdef _unbroadcast(g, shape):\n331\t    if g.shape == shape:\n332\t        return g\n333\t    _tick(g.size // 4)\n334\t    while g.ndim > len(shape):\n335\t        g = g.sum(0)\n336\t    axes = tuple(i for i, s in enumerate(shape) if s == 1 and g.shape[i] != 1)\n337\t    return g.sum(axes, keepdims=True) if axes else g\n338\t\n339\t\n340\tdef _floats(*ts):\n341\t    for t in ts:\n342\t        if t.is_int:\n343\t            raise RuleViolation(\"this op needs float tensors; convert with .float()\")\n344\t\n345\t\n346\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- creation\n347\t\n348\t\n349\tdef param(x):\n350\t    \"\"\"Mark a tensor as a trainable leaf.\"\"\"\n351\t    _train_only(\"param()\")\n352\t    _tick(x.size // 4)\n353\t    t = Tensor(_np.array(x._d, dtype=_F))\n354\t    t._rg = True\n355\t    return t\n356\t\n357\t\n358\tdef zeros(shape):\n359\t    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 16)\n360\t    return Tensor(_np.zeros(shape, _F))\n361\t\n362\t\n363\tdef ones(shape):\n364\t    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 8)\n365\t    return Tensor(_np.ones(shape, _F))\n366\t\n367\t\n368\tdef full(shape, value):\n369\t    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 8)\n370\t    return Tensor(_np.full(shape, float(value), _F))\n371\t\n372\t\n373\tdef arange(n):\n374\t    _tick(n // 4)\n375\t    return Tensor(_np.arange(n, dtype=_F))\n376\t\n377\t\n378\tdef randn(shape, std=1.0):\n379\t    _train_only(\"randn()\")\n380\t    _tick(4 * _np.prod(shape))\n381\t    return Tensor((_M.init_rng.standard_normal(shape, dtype=_F) * _F(std)).astype(_F))\n382\t\n383\t\n384\tdef rand(shape):\n385\t    _train_only(\"rand()\")\n386\t    _tick(2 * _np.prod(shape))\n387\t    return Tensor(_M.init_rng.random(shape, dtype=_F))\n388\t\n389\t\n390\tdef tril(x, k=0):\n391\t    \"\"\"Zero the elements above the k-th diagonal of the last two axes.\"\"\"\n392\t    _floats(x)\n393\t    _tick(2 * x.size)\n394\t    keep = _np.tril(_np.ones(x.shape[-2:], dtype=bool), k)\n395\t    out = _np.where(keep, x._d, _F(0))\n396\t\n397\t    def back(g, need):\n398\t        _tick(2 * g.size)\n399\t        return (_np.where(keep, g, _F(0)),)\n400\t\n401\t    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n402\t\n403\t\n404\tdef where(mask, a, b):\n405\t    \"\"\"mask is a float tensor of zeros and ones (from a comparison or tril).\"\"\"\n406\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n407\t    _floats(mask, a, b)\n408\t    m = mask._d != 0\n409\t    out = _np.where(m, a._d, b._d).astype(_F)\n410\t    _tick(2 * out.size)\n411\t\n412\t    def back(g, need):\n413\t        ga = gb = None\n414\t        if need[1]:\n415\t            _tick(2 * g.size)\n416\t            ga = _unbroadcast(_np.where(m, g, _F(0)), a.shape)\n417\t        if need[2]:\n418\t            _tick(2 * g.size)\n419\t            gb = _unbroadcast(_np.where(m, _F(0), g), b.shape)\n420\t        return (None, ga, gb)\n421\t\n422\t    return _make(out, (mask, a, b), back)\n423\t\n424\t\n425\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- elementwise\n426\t\n427\t\n428\tdef _unary(x, f, df, fwd=4, bwd=1):\n429\t    \"\"\"df(x_array, out_array, g) -> grad. fwd and bwd are prices in ticks per 4 elements.\"\"\"\n430\t    _floats(x)\n431\t    _tick(x.size * fwd // 4)\n432\t    xd = x._d\n433\t    out = f(xd).astype(_F, copy=False)\n434\t\n435\t    def back(g, need):\n436\t        _tick(g.size * bwd // 4)\n437\t        return (df(xd, out, g),)\n438\t\n439\t    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n440\t\n441\t\n442\tdef neg(x):\n443\t    return _unary(x, _np.negative, lambda x, y, g: -g, fwd=1)\n444\t\n445\t\n446\tdef exp(x):\n447\t    return _unary(x, _np.exp, lambda x, y, g: g * y)\n448\t\n449\t\n450\tdef log(x):\n451\t    return _unary(x, _np.log, lambda x, y, g: g / x, bwd=2)\n452\t\n453\t\n454\tdef sqrt(x):\n455\t    return _unary(x, _np.sqrt, lambda x, y, g: g * _F(0.5) / y, fwd=2, bwd=2)\n456\t\n457\t\n458\tdef rsqrt(x):\n459\t    return _unary(x, lambda a: 1 / _np.sqrt(a), lambda x, y, g: g * _F(-0.5) * y * y * y, fwd=2, bwd=2)\n460\t\n461\t\n462\tdef tanh(x):\n463\t    return _unary(x, _np.tanh, lambda x, y, g: g * (1 - y * y), fwd=2, bwd=4)\n464\t\n465\t\n466\tdef sigmoid(x):\n467\t    return _unary(x, lambda a: 1 / (1 + _np.exp(-a)), lambda x, y, g: g * y * (1 - y), bwd=2)\n468\t\n469\t\n470\tdef relu(x):\n471\t    return _unary(x, lambda a: _np.maximum(a, _F(0)), lambda x, y, g: g * (x > 0), fwd=2)\n472\t\n473\t\n474\tdef sin(x):\n475\t    return _unary(x, _np.sin, lambda x, y, g: g * _np.cos(x), bwd=4)\n476\t\n477\t\n478\tdef cos(x):\n479\t    return _unary(x, _np.cos, lambda x, y, g: -g * _np.sin(x), bwd=4)\n480\t\n481\t\n482\tdef abs(x):\n483\t    return _unary(x, _np.abs, lambda x, y, g: g * _np.sign(x), fwd=1, bwd=8)\n484\t\n485\t\n486\tdef sign(x):\n487\t    \"\"\"No gradient.\"\"\"\n488\t    _floats(x)\n489\t    _tick(x.size * 2)\n490\t    return Tensor(_np.sign(x._d).astype(_F))\n491\t\n492\t\n493\tdef power(x, p):\n494\t    if not isinstance(p, (int, float)) or isinstance(p, bool):\n495\t        raise RuleViolation(\"power() takes a number exponent\")\n496\t    return _unary(x, lambda a: _np.power(a, _F(p)), lambda x, y, g: g * _F(p) * _np.power(x, _F(p - 1)), fwd=8, bwd=8)\n497\t\n498\t\n499\tdef add(a, b):\n500\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n501\t    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n502\t        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.add)\n503\t    out = a._d + b._d\n504\t    _tick(out.size // 4)\n505\t\n506\t    def back(g, need):\n507\t        return (_unbroadcast(g, a.shape) if need[0] else None, _unbroadcast(g, b.shape) if need[1] else None)\n508\t\n509\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n510\t\n511\t\n512\tdef sub(a, b):\n513\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n514\t    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n515\t        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.subtract)\n516\t    out = a._d - b._d\n517\t    _tick(out.size // 4)\n518\t\n519\t    def back(g, need):\n520\t        gb = None\n521\t        if need[1]:\n522\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n523\t            gb = _unbroadcast(-g, b.shape)\n524\t        return (_unbroadcast(g, a.shape) if need[0] else None, gb)\n525\t\n526\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n527\t\n528\t\n529\tdef mul(a, b):\n530\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n531\t    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n532\t        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.multiply)\n533\t    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n534\t    out = ad * bd\n535\t    _tick(out.size // 4)\n536\t\n537\t    def back(g, need):\n538\t        ga = gb = None\n539\t        if need[0]:\n540\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n541\t            ga = _unbroadcast(g * bd, a.shape)\n542\t        if need[1]:\n543\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n544\t            gb = _unbroadcast(g * ad, b.shape)\n545\t        return (ga, gb)\n546\t\n547\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n548\t\n549\t\n550\tdef div(a, b):\n551\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n552\t    _floats(a, b)\n553\t    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n554\t    out = (ad / bd).astype(_F, copy=False)\n555\t    _tick(out.size // 2)\n556\t\n557\t    def back(g, need):\n558\t        ga = gb = None\n559\t        if need[0]:\n560\t            _tick(g.size // 2)\n561\t            ga = _unbroadcast(g / bd, a.shape)\n562\t        if need[1]:\n563\t            _tick(g.size)\n564\t            gb = _unbroadcast(-g * out / bd, b.shape)\n565\t        return (ga, gb)\n566\t\n567\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n568\t\n569\t\n570\tdef maximum(a, b):\n571\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n572\t    _floats(a, b)\n573\t    out = _np.maximum(a._d, b._d)\n574\t    _tick(out.size // 2)\n575\t    pick_a = a._d >= b._d\n576\t\n577\t    def back(g, need):\n578\t        ga = gb = None\n579\t        if need[0]:\n580\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n581\t            ga = _unbroadcast(g * pick_a, a.shape)\n582\t        if need[1]:\n583\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n584\t            gb = _unbroadcast(g * ~pick_a, b.shape)\n585\t        return (ga, gb)\n586\t\n587\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n588\t\n589\t\n590\tdef minimum(a, b):\n591\t    return neg(maximum(neg(a), neg(b)))\n592\t\n593\t\n594\tdef _compare(a, b, f):\n595\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b, a)\n596\t    out = f(a._d, b._d).astype(_F)\n597\t    _tick(out.size // 4)\n598\t    return Tensor(out)\n599\t\n600\t\n601\tdef _int_binary(a, b, f, per_4=1):\n602\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b, a)\n603\t    if not (a.is_int and b.is_int):\n604\t        raise RuleViolation(\"integer ops need two integer operands\")\n605\t    out = f(a._d, b._d).astype(_I)\n606\t    _tick(out.size * per_4 // 4)\n607\t    return Tensor(out)\n608\t\n609\t\n610\tdef to_float(x):\n611\t    _tick(x.size // 4)\n612\t    return Tensor(x._d.astype(_F))\n613\t\n614\t\n615\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- reductions\n616\t\n617\t\n618\tdef _norm_axis(axis, ndim):\n619\t    if axis is None:\n620\t        return tuple(range(ndim))\n621\t    axes = axis if isinstance(axis, tuple) else (axis,)\n622\t    return tuple(a % ndim for a in axes)\n623\t\n624\t\n625\tdef sum(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n626\t    _floats(x)\n627\t    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n628\t    out = x._d.sum(axis=axes, keepdims=keepdims, dtype=_F)\n629\t    _tick(x.size // 4)\n630\t\n631\t    def back(g, need):\n632\t        _tick(x.size // 8)\n633\t        gk = g if keepdims else _np.expand_dims(g, axes)\n634\t        return (_np.broadcast_to(gk, x.shape).astype(_F),)\n635\t\n636\t    return _make(_np.asarray(out, _F), (x,), back)\n637\t\n638\t\n639\tdef mean(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n640\t    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n641\t    n = int(_np.prod([x.shape[a] for a in axes]))\n642\t    return mul(sum(x, axis, keepdims), 1.0 / n)\n643\t\n644\t\n645\tdef max(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n646\t    _floats(x)\n647\t    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n648\t    out = x._d.max(axis=axes, keepdims=True)\n649\t    _tick(x.size // 4)\n650\t\n651\t    def back(g, need):\n652\t        _tick(x.size)\n653\t        gk = g if keepdims else _np.expand_dims(g, axes)\n654\t        hit = x._d == out\n655\t        return (hit * gk / hit.sum(axis=axes, keepdims=True),)\n656\t\n657\t    return _make(out if keepdims else out.squeeze(axes), (x,), back)\n658\t\n659\t\n660\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- shapes (views are free)\n661\t\n662\t\n663\tdef _reshaped(a, shape):\n664\t    out = a.reshape(shape)\n665\t    _tick(0 if _np.may_share_memory(out, a) else out.size)\n666\t    return out\n667\t\n668\t\n669\tdef reshape(x, *shape):\n670\t    if len(shape) == 1 and isinstance(shape[0], tuple):\n671\t        shape = shape[0]\n672\t    src = x.shape\n673\t    return _make(_reshaped(x._d, shape), (x,), lambda g, need: (_reshaped(g, src),))\n674\t\n675\t\n676\tdef transpose(x, *axes):\n677\t    if len(axes) == 1 and isinstance(axes[0], tuple):\n678\t        axes = axes[0]\n679\t    axes = axes or tuple(reversed(range(x.ndim)))\n680\t    inv = tuple(_np.argsort(axes))\n681\t    _tick()\n682\t    return _make(x._d.transpose(axes), (x,), lambda g, need: (g.transpose(inv),))\n683\t\n684\t\n685\tdef swapaxes(x, a, b):\n686\t    _tick()\n687\t    return _make(x._d.swapaxes(a, b), (x,), lambda g, need: (g.swapaxes(a, b),))\n688\t\n689\t\n690\tdef _check_basic_key(key):\n691\t    keys = key if isinstance(key, tuple) else (key,)\n692\t    for k in keys:\n693\t        if type(k) not in (int, slice, type(None), type(...)):\n694\t            raise RuleViolation(\"indexing takes ints, slices, None and ...; use embedding() to gather\")\n695\t\n696\t\n697\tdef getitem(x, key):\n698\t    _check_basic_key(key)\n699\t    _tick()\n700\t    out = x._d[key]\n701\t    src_shape = x.shape\n702\t\n703\t    def back(g, need):\n704\t        _tick(_np.prod(src_shape) // 16 + g.size // 4)\n705\t        full_g = _np.zeros(src_shape, _F)\n706\t        full_g[key] = g\n707\t        return (full_g,)\n708\t\n709\t    if x.is_int:\n710\t        return Tensor(out)\n711\t    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n712\t\n713\t\n714\tdef split(x, sections, axis=-1):\n715\t    \"\"\"Split into equal parts (a view; the backward is a concat).\"\"\"\n716\t    parts = _np.split(x._d, sections, axis=axis)\n717\t    _tick(_CALL * len(parts))\n718\t    outs = []\n719\t    for i, part in enumerate(parts):\n720\t\n721\t        def back(g, need, i=i):\n722\t            _tick(_np.prod(x.shape) // 4 + 512 * len(parts))\n723\t            full_g = [_np.zeros_like(p) for p in parts]\n724\t            full_g[i] = g\n725\t            return (_np.concatenate(full_g, axis=axis),)\n726\t\n727\t        outs.append(_make(part, (x,), back) if not x.is_int else Tensor(part))\n728\t    return outs\n729\t\n730\t\n731\tdef concat(ts, axis=-1):\n732\t    ts = list(ts)\n733\t    out = _np.concatenate([t._d for t in ts], axis=axis)\n734\t    _tick(out.size // 4 + 256 * len(ts))\n735\t    if all(t.is_int for t in ts):\n736\t        return Tensor(out)\n737\t    _floats(*ts)\n738\t    bounds = _np.cumsum([t.shape[axis] for t in ts])[:-1]\n739\t\n740\t    def back(g, need):\n741\t        _tick(1024 * len(ts))\n742\t        return tuple(_np.split(g, bounds, axis=axis))\n743\t\n744\t    return _make(out, tuple(ts), back)\n745\t\n746\t\n747\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- matmul\n748\t\n749\t\n750\tdef _matmul_price(rows, inner, cols, calls):\n751\t    # thin products run far below BLAS's peak rate, so short sides price as if they had 8 rows or columns and 64 inner\n752\t    return calls * ((rows if rows > 8 else 8) * (cols if cols > 8 else 8) * (inner if inner > 64 else 64) // 128 + 256)\n753\t\n754\t\n755\tdef matmul(a, b):\n756\t    _floats(a, b)\n757\t    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n758\t    if ad.ndim < 2 or bd.ndim < 2:\n759\t        raise RuleViolation(\"matmul() needs tensors with at least two dimensions\")\n760\t    m, k, n = ad.shape[-2], ad.shape[-1], bd.shape[-1]\n761\t    calls = int(_np.prod(_np.broadcast_shapes(ad.shape[:-2], bd.shape[:-2])))\n762\t    if bd.ndim == 2:\n763\t        m, calls = m * calls, 1\n764\t    _tick(_matmul_price(m, k, n, calls))  # before the work, because time here is not bounded by memory\n765\t    if bd.ndim == 2 and ad.ndim > 2:\n766\t        lead = ad.shape[:-1]\n767\t        out = (ad.reshape(-1, ad.shape[-1]) @ bd).reshape(*lead, bd.shape[-1])\n768\t    else:\n769\t        out = ad @ bd\n770\t\n771\t    def back(g, need):\n772\t        ga = gb = None\n773\t        if need[0]:\n774\t            _tick(_matmul_price(m, n, k, calls))\n775\t            if bd.ndim == 2:\n776\t                ga = (g.reshape(-1, g.shape[-1]) @ bd.T).reshape(ad.shape)\n777\t            else:\n778\t                ga = _unbroadcast(g @ _np.swapaxes(bd, -1, -2), ad.shape)\n779\t        if need[1]:\n780\t            _tick(_matmul_price(k, m, n, calls))\n781\t            if bd.ndim == 2:\n782\t                gb = ad.reshape(-1, k).T @ g.reshape(-1, g.shape[-1])\n783\t            else:\n784\t                gb = _unbroadcast(_np.swapaxes(ad, -1, -2) @ g, bd.shape)\n785\t        return (ga, gb)\n786\t\n787\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n788\t\n789\t\n790\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- indexing\n791\t\n792\t\n793\tdef embedding(table, idx):\n794\t    \"\"\"Rows of a 2-D table picked by an integer tensor: out[...] = table[idx[...]].\"\"\"\n795\t    _floats(table)\n796\t    if not idx.is_int:\n797\t        raise RuleViolation(\"embedding() needs an integer index tensor\")\n798\t    ix = idx._d\n799\t    if ix.size and (ix.min() < 0 or ix.max() >= table.shape[0]):\n800\t        raise RuleViolation(\"embedding index out of range\")\n801\t    out = table._d[ix]\n802\t    _tick((8 + table.size // (1 << 19)) * ix.size + out.size // 4)  # bigger tables miss the cache on more rows\n803\t    rows = table.shape\n804\t\n805\t    def back(g, need):\n806\t        _tick(16 * g.size + table.size // 16)\n807\t        gt = _np.zeros(rows, _F)\n808\t        _np.add.at(gt, ix.reshape(-1), g.reshape(-1, rows[1]))\n809\t        return (gt, None)\n810\t\n811\t    return _make(out, (table, idx), back)\n812\t\n813\t\n814\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fused\n815\t\n816\t\n817\tdef softmax(x, axis=-1):\n818\t    _floats(x)\n819\t    _tick(2 * x.size)\n820\t    z = x._d - x._d.max(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n821\t    e = _np.exp(z)\n822\t    y = e / e.sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n823\t\n824\t    def back(g, need):\n825\t        _tick(x.size)\n826\t        return (y * (g - (g * y).sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True)),)\n827\t\n828\t    return _make(y.astype(_F, copy=False), (x,), back)\n829\t\n830\t\n831\tdef log_softmax(x, axis=-1):\n832\t    _floats(x)\n833\t    _tick(2 * x.size)\n834\t    z = x._d - x._d.max(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n835\t    lse = _np.log(_np.exp(z).sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True))\n836\t    y = z - lse\n837\t\n838\t    def back(g, need):\n839\t        _tick(x.size)\n840\t        return (g - _np.exp(y) * g.sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True),)\n841\t\n842\t    return _make(y.astype(_F, copy=False), (x,), back)\n843\t\n844\t\n845\tdef cross_entropy(logits, targets):\n846\t    \"\"\"Mean negative log-likelihood in nats. logits (..., V) float, targets (...) int.\"\"\"\n847\t    _floats(logits)\n848\t    if not targets.is_int:\n849\t        raise RuleViolation(\"cross_entropy() needs integer targets\")\n850\t    V = logits.shape[-1]\n851\t    z = logits._d.reshape(-1, V)\n852\t    t = targets._d.reshape(-1)\n853\t    _tick(2 * z.size + _CALL)\n854\t    zmax = z.max(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n855\t    e = _np.exp(z - zmax)\n856\t    s = e.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n857\t    n = z.shape[0]\n858\t    nll = (_np.log(s[:, 0]) + zmax[:, 0] - z[_np.arange(n), t]).mean()\n859\t\n860\t    def back(g, need):\n861\t        _tick(z.size)\n862\t        p = e / s\n863\t        p[_np.arange(n), t] -= 1\n864\t        return ((p * (g / n)).reshape(logits.shape).astype(_F, copy=False), None)\n865\t\n866\t    return _make(_np.asarray(nll, _F), (logits, targets), back)\n867\t"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8639e370-419a-4235-bc26-65617a606019", "uuid": "19114f08-fc9e-4b82-8d3c-6e9696560a5e", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T17:19:37.671Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/home/user/att/attempt-04/odometer/_engine.py", "content": "\"\"\"The metered tensor engine.\n\nEvery engine call advances one global odometer by a price that is a function of tensor shapes only, never of the\nmachine or the values, so the same program reaches the same reading everywhere.\n\nThe unit is a tick, priced to be about one nanosecond of one laptop core. tools/calibrate.py measures nanoseconds per\ntick for every op on real machines and fails if any op drifts more than a factor of 5 from the median, so an entry\ncannot get cheap work by picking mispriced ops.\n\nPrices (v3), per call:\n  * every call: 2000 ticks, the Python overhead of the call itself. Backward passes pay it again per node.\n  * matmul of (..., m, k) @ (..., k, n): max(m, 8) * max(k, 64) * max(n, 8) / 128 plus 256, per batch element (a 2-D right side is one\n    flat call, so m counts the batch and the 256 is paid once). The same again per input needing a gradient, with the\n    inner and outer dimensions swapped to match the product backward actually does.\n  * cheap elementwise work (add, mul, negate, compare, copy, sum): 1 tick per 4 elements. ones and full 1 per 8, and\n    zeros and the backward of a sum 1 per 16 and 1 per 8, because they only fill memory.\n  * sqrt, div, tanh: 1 tick per 2 elements. exp, log, sigmoid, sin, cos: 1 per element. where, power, sign: 2 per\n    element. Integer % and //: 1 per element.\n  * randn 4 and rand 2 per element. Logit ops (softmax, log_softmax, cross_entropy): 2 per logit, 1 per logit backward;\n    cross_entropy pays the call price twice.\n  * embedding: 1 per 4 elements, plus per row 8 and 2 per million table floats; backward 16 per element plus the zeroed\n    table.\n  * concat: 256 per input tensor on top of the elements, 1024 per input tensor backward. split: 2000 per part forward,\n    512 per part backward. data.batch: 2000 plus 64 per row plus 1 per byte.\n  * views (transpose, slicing, a reshape that keeps the memory) are free apart from the call price. A reshape that has\n    to copy pays 1 per element.\n\nWhen a charge would pass the budget, the op raises BudgetExhausted and every later op raises too.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport contextlib as _contextlib\nimport math as _math\n\nimport numpy as _np\n\n_F = _np.float32\n_I = _np.int32\n\n\nclass BudgetExhausted(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\nclass RuleViolation(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\nclass _Meter:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.reset(None, 0)\n\n    def reset(self, budget, seed, mode=\"train\", item_cap=20_000):\n        self.budget = budget\n        self.used = 0\n        self.exhausted = False\n        self.mode = mode\n        self.grad = mode == \"train\"\n        self.items = 0\n        self.item_cap = item_cap\n        self.init_rng = _np.random.default_rng([seed, 0])\n        self.data_rng = _np.random.default_rng([seed, 1])\n\n\n_M = _Meter()\n\n\n_CALL = 2000  # ticks for one engine call, whatever its size\n\n\ndef _tick(n=0):\n    if _M.exhausted:\n        raise BudgetExhausted(\"the odometer already reached its budget\")\n    n = int(n) if n > 0 else 0  # a negative price would run the odometer backwards\n    n += _CALL\n    if _M.budget is not None and _M.used + n > _M.budget:\n        _M.exhausted = True\n        raise BudgetExhausted(f\"budget {_M.budget:.3e} reached at {_M.used:.3e}\")\n    _M.used += n\n\n\ndef _train_only(what):\n    if _M.mode != \"train\":\n        raise RuleViolation(f\"{what} is not allowed during evaluation\")\n\n\ndef used():\n    return _M.used\n\n\ndef budget():\n    return _M.budget\n\n\ndef remaining():\n    return None if _M.budget is None else _M.budget - _M.used\n\n\n@_contextlib.contextmanager\ndef no_grad():\n    prev = _M.grad\n    _M.grad = False\n    try:\n        yield\n    finally:\n        _M.grad = prev\n\n\nclass Tensor:\n    \"\"\"An opaque array. Values leave the engine only through item(), which is rationed.\"\"\"\n\n    __slots__ = (\"_d\", \"_prev\", \"_back\", \"_rg\", \"grad\")\n\n    def __init__(self, d, prev=(), back=None, rg=False):\n        self._d = d\n        self._prev = prev\n        self._back = back\n        self._rg = rg\n        self.grad = None\n\n    # ---- what an entry may know about a tensor\n    @property\n    def shape(self):\n        return self._d.shape\n\n    @property\n    def ndim(self):\n        return self._d.ndim\n\n    @property\n    def size(self):\n        return int(self._d.size)\n\n    @property\n    def is_int(self):\n        return self._d.dtype.kind == \"i\"\n\n    @property\n    def requires_grad(self):\n        return self._rg\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return self._d.shape[0]\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        kind = \"int\" if self.is_int else \"float\"\n        return f\"Tensor(shape={self.shape}, {kind})\"\n\n    __str__ = __repr__\n\n    def __format__(self, spec):\n        return repr(self)\n\n    def __bool__(self):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"a tensor has no truth value; use item()\")\n\n    def __float__(self):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"use item() to read a scalar\")\n\n    __int__ = __index__ = __float__\n\n    def __iter__(self):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"tensors are not iterable\")\n\n    def __array__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"tensors cannot be converted to arrays\")\n\n    __hash__ = object.__hash__\n\n    def item(self):\n        _train_only(\"item()\")\n        if self._d.size != 1:\n            raise RuleViolation(\"item() needs a one-element tensor\")\n        _M.items += 1\n        if _M.items > _M.item_cap:\n            raise RuleViolation(f\"more than {_M.item_cap} item() reads\")\n        _tick()\n        return self._d.item()\n\n    def detach(self):\n        return Tensor(self._d)\n\n    # ---- in-place update of a parameter (optimizers)\n    def update(self, value):\n        _train_only(\"update()\")\n        value = _as_tensor(value, self)\n        if value.shape != self.shape:\n            value = Tensor(_np.broadcast_to(value._d, self.shape))\n        _tick(self.size // 4)\n        self._d[...] = value._d\n\n    # ---- autodiff\n    def backward(self):\n        _train_only(\"backward()\")\n        if self.size != 1:\n            raise RuleViolation(\"backward() needs a scalar loss\")\n        order, seen, stack = [], set(), [(self, False)]\n        while stack:\n            node, done = stack.pop()\n            if done:\n                order.append(node)\n                continue\n            if id(node) in seen or not node._rg:\n                continue\n            seen.add(id(node))\n            stack.append((node, True))\n            for p in node._prev:\n                stack.append((p, False))\n        grads = {id(self): _np.ones_like(self._d)}\n        for node in reversed(order):\n            g = grads.pop(id(node), None)\n            if g is None:\n                continue\n            if node._back is None:\n                if node.grad is None:\n                    node.grad = Tensor(g.astype(_F, copy=False))\n                else:\n                    _tick(g.size // 4)\n                    node.grad._d = node.grad._d + g\n                continue\n            _tick()\n            need = [p._rg for p in node._prev]\n            for p, pg in zip(node._prev, node._back(g, need)):\n                if pg is None or not p._rg:\n                    continue\n                if id(p) in grads:\n                    _tick(pg.size // 4)\n                    grads[id(p)] = grads[id(p)] + pg\n                else:\n                    grads[id(p)] = pg\n            node._prev, node._back = (), None\n\n    # ---- operators\n    def __add__(self, o):\n        return add(self, o)\n\n    def __radd__(self, o):\n        return add(o, self)\n\n    def __sub__(self, o):\n        return sub(self, o)\n\n    def __rsub__(self, o):\n        return sub(o, self)\n\n    def __mul__(self, o):\n        return mul(self, o)\n\n    def __rmul__(self, o):\n        return mul(o, self)\n\n    def __truediv__(self, o):\n        return div(self, o)\n\n    def __rtruediv__(self, o):\n        return div(o, self)\n\n    def __neg__(self):\n        return neg(self)\n\n    def __pow__(self, p):\n        return power(self, p)\n\n    def __matmul__(self, o):\n        return matmul(self, o)\n\n    def __mod__(self, o):\n        return _int_binary(self, o, _np.mod, per_4=4)\n\n    def __floordiv__(self, o):\n        return _int_binary(self, o, _np.floor_divide, per_4=4)\n\n    def __gt__(self, o):\n        return _compare(self, o, _np.greater)\n\n    def __ge__(self, o):\n        return _compare(self, o, _np.greater_equal)\n\n    def __lt__(self, o):\n        return _compare(self, o, _np.less)\n\n    def __le__(self, o):\n        return _compare(self, o, _np.less_equal)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, key):\n        return getitem(self, key)\n\n    def reshape(self, *shape):\n        return reshape(self, *shape)\n\n    def transpose(self, *axes):\n        return transpose(self, *axes)\n\n    def swapaxes(self, a, b):\n        return swapaxes(self, a, b)\n\n    def sum(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n        return sum(self, axis, keepdims)\n\n    def mean(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n        return mean(self, axis, keepdims)\n\n    def max(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n        return max(self, axis, keepdims)\n\n    def float(self):\n        return to_float(self)\n\n    @property\n    def T(self):\n        return swapaxes(self, -1, -2)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- helpers\n\n\ndef _as_tensor(x, like=None):\n    if isinstance(x, Tensor):\n        return x\n    if isinstance(x, bool) or not isinstance(x, (int, float)):\n        raise RuleViolation(f\"expected a tensor or a number, got {type(x).__name__}\")\n    dtype = _I if (like is not None and like.is_int and isinstance(x, int)) else _F\n    return Tensor(_np.asarray(x, dtype=dtype))\n\n\ndef _make(d, parents, back):\n    rg = _M.grad and any(p._rg for p in parents)\n    return Tensor(d, parents if rg else (), back if rg else None, rg)\n\n\ndef _unbroadcast(g, shape):\n    if g.shape == shape:\n        return g\n    _tick(g.size // 4)\n    while g.ndim > len(shape):\n        g = g.sum(0)\n    axes = tuple(i for i, s in enumerate(shape) if s == 1 and g.shape[i] != 1)\n    return g.sum(axes, keepdims=True) if axes else g\n\n\ndef _floats(*ts):\n    for t in ts:\n        if t.is_int:\n            raise RuleViolation(\"this op needs float tensors; convert with .float()\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- creation\n\n\ndef param(x):\n    \"\"\"Mark a tensor as a trainable leaf.\"\"\"\n    _train_only(\"param()\")\n    _tick(x.size // 4)\n    t = Tensor(_np.array(x._d, dtype=_F))\n    t._rg = True\n    return t\n\n\ndef zeros(shape):\n    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 16)\n    return Tensor(_np.zeros(shape, _F))\n\n\ndef ones(shape):\n    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 8)\n    return Tensor(_np.ones(shape, _F))\n\n\ndef full(shape, value):\n    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 8)\n    return Tensor(_np.full(shape, float(value), _F))\n\n\ndef arange(n):\n    _tick(n // 4)\n    return Tensor(_np.arange(n, dtype=_F))\n\n\ndef randn(shape, std=1.0):\n    _train_only(\"randn()\")\n    _tick(4 * _np.prod(shape))\n    return Tensor((_M.init_rng.standard_normal(shape, dtype=_F) * _F(std)).astype(_F))\n\n\ndef rand(shape):\n    _train_only(\"rand()\")\n    _tick(2 * _np.prod(shape))\n    return Tensor(_M.init_rng.random(shape, dtype=_F))\n\n\ndef tril(x, k=0):\n    \"\"\"Zero the elements above the k-th diagonal of the last two axes.\"\"\"\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(2 * x.size)\n    keep = _np.tril(_np.ones(x.shape[-2:], dtype=bool), k)\n    out = _np.where(keep, x._d, _F(0))\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(2 * g.size)\n        return (_np.where(keep, g, _F(0)),)\n\n    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n\n\ndef where(mask, a, b):\n    \"\"\"mask is a float tensor of zeros and ones (from a comparison or tril).\"\"\"\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n    _floats(mask, a, b)\n    m = mask._d != 0\n    out = _np.where(m, a._d, b._d).astype(_F)\n    _tick(2 * out.size)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(2 * g.size)\n            ga = _unbroadcast(_np.where(m, g, _F(0)), a.shape)\n        if need[2]:\n            _tick(2 * g.size)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(_np.where(m, _F(0), g), b.shape)\n        return (None, ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (mask, a, b), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- elementwise\n\n\ndef _unary(x, f, df, fwd=4, bwd=1):\n    \"\"\"df(x_array, out_array, g) -> grad. fwd and bwd are prices in ticks per 4 elements.\"\"\"\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(x.size * fwd // 4)\n    xd = x._d\n    out = f(xd).astype(_F, copy=False)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(g.size * bwd // 4)\n        return (df(xd, out, g),)\n\n    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n\n\ndef neg(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.negative, lambda x, y, g: -g, fwd=1)\n\n\ndef exp(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.exp, lambda x, y, g: g * y)\n\n\ndef log(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.log, lambda x, y, g: g / x, bwd=2)\n\n\ndef sqrt(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.sqrt, lambda x, y, g: g * _F(0.5) / y, fwd=2, bwd=2)\n\n\ndef rsqrt(x):\n    return _unary(x, lambda a: 1 / _np.sqrt(a), lambda x, y, g: g * _F(-0.5) * y * y * y, fwd=2, bwd=2)\n\n\ndef tanh(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.tanh, lambda x, y, g: g * (1 - y * y), fwd=2, bwd=4)\n\n\ndef sigmoid(x):\n    return _unary(x, lambda a: 1 / (1 + _np.exp(-a)), lambda x, y, g: g * y * (1 - y), bwd=2)\n\n\ndef relu(x):\n    return _unary(x, lambda a: _np.maximum(a, _F(0)), lambda x, y, g: g * (x > 0), fwd=2)\n\n\ndef sin(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.sin, lambda x, y, g: g * _np.cos(x), bwd=4)\n\n\ndef cos(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.cos, lambda x, y, g: -g * _np.sin(x), bwd=4)\n\n\ndef abs(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.abs, lambda x, y, g: g * _np.sign(x), fwd=1, bwd=8)\n\n\ndef sign(x):\n    \"\"\"No gradient.\"\"\"\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(x.size * 2)\n    return Tensor(_np.sign(x._d).astype(_F))\n\n\ndef power(x, p):\n    if not isinstance(p, (int, float)) or isinstance(p, bool):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"power() takes a number exponent\")\n    return _unary(x, lambda a: _np.power(a, _F(p)), lambda x, y, g: g * _F(p) * _np.power(x, _F(p - 1)), fwd=8, bwd=8)\n\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.add)\n    out = a._d + b._d\n    _tick(out.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        return (_unbroadcast(g, a.shape) if need[0] else None, _unbroadcast(g, b.shape) if need[1] else None)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef sub(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.subtract)\n    out = a._d - b._d\n    _tick(out.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        gb = None\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(-g, b.shape)\n        return (_unbroadcast(g, a.shape) if need[0] else None, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef mul(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.multiply)\n    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n    out = ad * bd\n    _tick(out.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[0]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            ga = _unbroadcast(g * bd, a.shape)\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(g * ad, b.shape)\n        return (ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef div(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n    _floats(a, b)\n    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n    out = (ad / bd).astype(_F, copy=False)\n    _tick(out.size // 2)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[0]:\n            _tick(g.size // 2)\n            ga = _unbroadcast(g / bd, a.shape)\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(g.size)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(-g * out / bd, b.shape)\n        return (ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef maximum(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n    _floats(a, b)\n    out = _np.maximum(a._d, b._d)\n    _tick(out.size // 2)\n    pick_a = a._d >= b._d\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[0]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            ga = _unbroadcast(g * pick_a, a.shape)\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(g * ~pick_a, b.shape)\n        return (ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef minimum(a, b):\n    return neg(maximum(neg(a), neg(b)))\n\n\ndef _compare(a, b, f):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    out = f(a._d, b._d).astype(_F)\n    _tick(out.size // 4)\n    return Tensor(out)\n\n\ndef _int_binary(a, b, f, per_4=1):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    if not (a.is_int and b.is_int):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"integer ops need two integer operands\")\n    out = f(a._d, b._d).astype(_I)\n    _tick(out.size * per_4 // 4)\n    return Tensor(out)\n\n\ndef to_float(x):\n    _tick(x.size // 4)\n    return Tensor(x._d.astype(_F))\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- reductions\n\n\ndef _norm_axis(axis, ndim):\n    if axis is None:\n        return tuple(range(ndim))\n    axes = axis if isinstance(axis, tuple) else (axis,)\n    return tuple(a % ndim for a in axes)\n\n\ndef sum(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n    _floats(x)\n    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n    out = x._d.sum(axis=axes, keepdims=keepdims, dtype=_F)\n    _tick(x.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(x.size // 8)\n        gk = g if keepdims else _np.expand_dims(g, axes)\n        return (_np.broadcast_to(gk, x.shape).astype(_F),)\n\n    return _make(_np.asarray(out, _F), (x,), back)\n\n\ndef mean(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n    n = int(_np.prod([x.shape[a] for a in axes]))\n    return mul(sum(x, axis, keepdims), 1.0 / n)\n\n\ndef max(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n    _floats(x)\n    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n    out = x._d.max(axis=axes, keepdims=True)\n    _tick(x.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(x.size)\n        gk = g if keepdims else _np.expand_dims(g, axes)\n        hit = x._d == out\n        return (hit * gk / hit.sum(axis=axes, keepdims=True),)\n\n    return _make(out if keepdims else out.squeeze(axes), (x,), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- shapes (views are free)\n\n\ndef _reshaped(a, shape):\n    out = a.reshape(shape)\n    _tick(0 if _np.may_share_memory(out, a) else out.size)\n    return out\n\n\ndef reshape(x, *shape):\n    if len(shape) == 1 and isinstance(shape[0], tuple):\n        shape = shape[0]\n    src = x.shape\n    return _make(_reshaped(x._d, shape), (x,), lambda g, need: (_reshaped(g, src),))\n\n\ndef transpose(x, *axes):\n    if len(axes) == 1 and isinstance(axes[0], tuple):\n        axes = axes[0]\n    axes = axes or tuple(reversed(range(x.ndim)))\n    inv = tuple(_np.argsort(axes))\n    _tick()\n    return _make(x._d.transpose(axes), (x,), lambda g, need: (g.transpose(inv),))\n\n\ndef swapaxes(x, a, b):\n    _tick()\n    return _make(x._d.swapaxes(a, b), (x,), lambda g, need: (g.swapaxes(a, b),))\n\n\ndef _check_basic_key(key):\n    keys = key if isinstance(key, tuple) else (key,)\n    for k in keys:\n        if type(k) not in (int, slice, type(None), type(...)):\n            raise RuleViolation(\"indexing takes ints, slices, None and ...; use embedding() to gather\")\n\n\ndef getitem(x, key):\n    _check_basic_key(key)\n    _tick()\n    out = x._d[key]\n    src_shape = x.shape\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(_np.prod(src_shape) // 16 + g.size // 4)\n        full_g = _np.zeros(src_shape, _F)\n        full_g[key] = g\n        return (full_g,)\n\n    if x.is_int:\n        return Tensor(out)\n    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n\n\ndef split(x, sections, axis=-1):\n    \"\"\"Split into equal parts (a view; the backward is a concat).\"\"\"\n    parts = _np.split(x._d, sections, axis=axis)\n    _tick(_CALL * len(parts))\n    outs = []\n    for i, part in enumerate(parts):\n\n        def back(g, need, i=i):\n            _tick(_np.prod(x.shape) // 4 + 512 * len(parts))\n            full_g = [_np.zeros_like(p) for p in parts]\n            full_g[i] = g\n            return (_np.concatenate(full_g, axis=axis),)\n\n        outs.append(_make(part, (x,), back) if not x.is_int else Tensor(part))\n    return outs\n\n\ndef concat(ts, axis=-1):\n    ts = list(ts)\n    out = _np.concatenate([t._d for t in ts], axis=axis)\n    _tick(out.size // 4 + 256 * len(ts))\n    if all(t.is_int for t in ts):\n        return Tensor(out)\n    _floats(*ts)\n    bounds = _np.cumsum([t.shape[axis] for t in ts])[:-1]\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(1024 * len(ts))\n        return tuple(_np.split(g, bounds, axis=axis))\n\n    return _make(out, tuple(ts), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- matmul\n\n\ndef _matmul_price(rows, inner, cols, calls):\n    # thin products run far below BLAS's peak rate, so short sides price as if they had 8 rows or columns and 64 inner\n    return calls * ((rows if rows > 8 else 8) * (cols if cols > 8 else 8) * (inner if inner > 64 else 64) // 128 + 256)\n\n\ndef matmul(a, b):\n    _floats(a, b)\n    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n    if ad.ndim < 2 or bd.ndim < 2:\n        raise RuleViolation(\"matmul() needs tensors with at least two dimensions\")\n    m, k, n = ad.shape[-2], ad.shape[-1], bd.shape[-1]\n    calls = int(_np.prod(_np.broadcast_shapes(ad.shape[:-2], bd.shape[:-2])))\n    if bd.ndim == 2:\n        m, calls = m * calls, 1\n    _tick(_matmul_price(m, k, n, calls))  # before the work, because time here is not bounded by memory\n    if bd.ndim == 2 and ad.ndim > 2:\n        lead = ad.shape[:-1]\n        out = (ad.reshape(-1, ad.shape[-1]) @ bd).reshape(*lead, bd.shape[-1])\n    else:\n        out = ad @ bd\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[0]:\n            _tick(_matmul_price(m, n, k, calls))\n            if bd.ndim == 2:\n                ga = (g.reshape(-1, g.shape[-1]) @ bd.T).reshape(ad.shape)\n            else:\n                ga = _unbroadcast(g @ _np.swapaxes(bd, -1, -2), ad.shape)\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(_matmul_price(k, m, n, calls))\n            if bd.ndim == 2:\n                gb = ad.reshape(-1, k).T @ g.reshape(-1, g.shape[-1])\n            else:\n                gb = _unbroadcast(_np.swapaxes(ad, -1, -2) @ g, bd.shape)\n        return (ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- indexing\n\n\ndef embedding(table, idx):\n    \"\"\"Rows of a 2-D table picked by an integer tensor: out[...] = table[idx[...]].\"\"\"\n    _floats(table)\n    if not idx.is_int:\n        raise RuleViolation(\"embedding() needs an integer index tensor\")\n    ix = idx._d\n    if ix.size and (ix.min() < 0 or ix.max() >= table.shape[0]):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"embedding index out of range\")\n    out = table._d[ix]\n    _tick((8 + table.size // (1 << 19)) * ix.size + out.size // 4)  # bigger tables miss the cache on more rows\n    rows = table.shape\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(16 * g.size + table.size // 16)\n        gt = _np.zeros(rows, _F)\n        _np.add.at(gt, ix.reshape(-1), g.reshape(-1, rows[1]))\n        return (gt, None)\n\n    return _make(out, (table, idx), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fused\n\n\ndef softmax(x, axis=-1):\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(2 * x.size)\n    z = x._d - x._d.max(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n    e = _np.exp(z)\n    y = e / e.sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(x.size)\n        return (y * (g - (g * y).sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True)),)\n\n    return _make(y.astype(_F, copy=False), (x,), back)\n\n\ndef log_softmax(x, axis=-1):\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(2 * x.size)\n    z = x._d - x._d.max(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n    lse = _np.log(_np.exp(z).sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True))\n    y = z - lse\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(x.size)\n        return (g - _np.exp(y) * g.sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True),)\n\n    return _make(y.astype(_F, copy=False), (x,), back)\n\n\ndef cross_entropy(logits, targets):\n    \"\"\"Mean negative log-likelihood in nats. logits (..., V) float, targets (...) int.\"\"\"\n    _floats(logits)\n    if not targets.is_int:\n        raise RuleViolation(\"cross_entropy() needs integer targets\")\n    V = logits.shape[-1]\n    z = logits._d.reshape(-1, V)\n    t = targets._d.reshape(-1)\n    _tick(2 * z.size + _CALL)\n    zmax = z.max(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    e = _np.exp(z - zmax)\n    s = e.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    n = z.shape[0]\n    nll = (_np.log(s[:, 0]) + zmax[:, 0] - z[_np.arange(n), t]).mean()\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(z.size)\n        p = e / s\n        p[_np.arange(n), t] -= 1\n        return ((p * (g / n)).reshape(logits.shape).astype(_F, copy=False), None)\n\n    return _make(_np.asarray(nll, _F), (logits, targets), back)\n", "numLines": 867, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 867}}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Nre68uyxBgD9ZkcHvYJDZW", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
