{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgeXMXGTSvfidDYx1tkmo", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I submitted one claim, which beats the record on dev: **1.0991 bpb against 1.1082**, mean of 8 fresh seeds (SD 0.0012, 95% CI ±0.0010). That's a gain of 0.0091, well past the 0.002 margin the verifier requires for a new record. It's in `claims/1/`, and none of my other variants earned a second claim.\n\n**What changed from the record:**\n1. **Cheaper low-order tables:** orders 1–3 pay for the embedding backward on every 4th step and order 4 on every 2nd, after the first 15% of the run. That backward is most of a step's price, so the higher orders see more bytes for the same ticks.\n2. **Word-keyed in-window stages:** two new stages use the case-folded current word prefix, and that prefix plus the previous word.\n3. **Story-aware votes:** a vote from before the last story boundary in the window counts 0.1, because it comes from a different story.\n\n**How far to trust the number:**\n- **Selection bias:** the 8 seeds were fresh and played no part in choosing this variant. It had scored 1.0973 on the seed that selected it, out of about 20 variants tried on one seed each, so I claimed 1.0991 rather than that figure.\n- **Final file checked:** its code is identical to the tested variant apart from the docstring, and it reproduces 1.0973 on that seed.\n- **Record on this machine:** two seeds of the unmodified record gave 1.1092 and 1.1097, slightly above its published 1.1082. The gain over the published figure may therefore be a little understated.\n- **Credit for each change:** I never tested the three changes separately at 8 seeds. Each helped on its single seed, but those differences are close to seed noise. The 0.1 vote weight isn't separated from 0 or 0.25.\n- **Sealed split:** it uses different windows from dev, so the verifier's mean could differ from 1.0991 by more than seed noise. I couldn't measure that here.\n\n**Tried without gain:**\n- **Word contexts as tables:** worse than the record, at 1.1118–1.1239.\n- **Sampling orders 5 and 6 as well:** worse, at 1.1030.\n- **Freezing the tables late:** no gain, at 1.1013.\n- **Position features for the gate:** no gain, at 1.0992.\n- **Recency-decayed votes:** no gain alone (1.1090, against about 1.1082 for the record).\n- **Wider hidden layer:** first looked good at 1.0971, but two more seeds gave 1.1000 and 1.1005.\n- **Extra stages plus a bigger gate:** each looked good alone at about 1.0975, but together gave 1.0993 and 1.1000.\n- **Resetting hashes at story boundaries:** 1.0998 over 4 seeds.\n\nI didn't use the open holes listed in `tests/attacks/README.md`, and the entry stays within the static rules and the price caps. My experiment scripts and logs are in `work/`."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1446, "cache_read_input_tokens": 121313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1446}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8639e370-419a-4235-bc26-65617a606019", "uuid": "12fc6dd7-a4e1-4556-a645-bd95c82c2e3f", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T17:50:07.393Z", "request_id": "req_011CgeXMWpuSPBJWpdheYhih"}
